# Construction editor overflow scrolling

Ensure ordered construction plans remain fully editable when their rows exceed the available screen height.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] The construction editor scrolls vertically when ordered rows extend below the viewport.
- [x] Every construction row can be reached without being obscured permanently by the bottom action bar.
- [x] The final-step bin, Clear, preview, and New Step controls remain reachable and interactive.
- [x] The top player selector and preview placement remain consistent with SCR-004 while content scrolls beneath or below them as designed.
- [x] Cancel and Save remain fixed, visible, and interactive throughout scrolling.
- [x] Adding a step does not strand the new final row outside reachable scroll bounds.
- [x] Cards-plan scrolling and layout remain unchanged.
- [x] Overflow regression coverage compiles with a twelve-step ordered fixture.
- [ ] Focused UI checks pass on a functioning simulator.

## Scope notes

- The editor already contains a ScrollView; this task owns layout, insets, and regression behavior required for real overflow rather than replacing the navigation model.

## Evidence

- Wrapped the editor ScrollView in `ScrollViewReader`, added bottom clearance above the fixed action inset, and retained the fixed top selector/preview overlay.
- Newly appended construction steps animate-scroll to a stable bottom anchor after returning from placement; removals do not force-scroll.
- Cards retain the same content path and receive no construction-specific auto-scroll behavior.
- Added a deterministic twelve-step ordered overflow fixture with stable unique row identities.
- The complete app and test bundles compile using `/private/tmp/Catanalyst-tasks025-030-derived`.
